{"name":"Woodland Wonder","hex":"#0d6323","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woodland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a creature or object: growing, living, or existing in a woodland.","Having the character of a woodland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Land covered with woody vegetation.","A low-density forest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woodland"},{"term":"wonder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sense of awe, astonishment and curiosity, inspired by unexpected events, novel experiences and inexplicable circumstances, sometimes accompanied by surprise, shock or reverence.","Something that causes amazement or awe; a marvel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be affected with surprise or admiration; to be struck with astonishment; to be amazed; to marvel; often followed by at.","To ponder; to feel doubt and curiosity; to query in the mind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woodland","blocks":[{"text":"A woodland is, in the broad sense, land covered with woody plants, or in a narrow sense, synonymous with wood, a low-density forest forming open habitats with plenty of sunlight and limited shade. Some savannas may also be woodlands, such as savanna woodland, where trees and shrubs form a light canopy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg/330px-Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodland","wikidata":"Q3241565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/500px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/1280px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa